1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
DappGo existed before this hackathon.

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:05,150
This verifier, its site and every piece of

3
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:08,700
evidence were built between
October 27 and November 4.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,000
A finance post goes viral.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,533
Thousands repost it.

6
00:00:12,533 --> 00:00:13,466
Is it right?

7
00:00:13,466 --> 00:00:17,333
This one has a real number
— and the wrong period.

8
00:00:17,333 --> 00:00:21,700
Numbers like this move money,
and wrong numbers lose it.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,466
And it's not just text.

10
00:00:24,466 --> 00:00:25,766
Screenshots,

11
00:00:25,766 --> 00:00:30,533
PDFs, podcasts, videos
— numbers everywhere.

12
00:00:30,533 --> 00:00:33,700
How do you check all of them?

13
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,866
Asking a model directly
gets one in five right.

14
00:00:38,866 --> 00:00:45,000
Give the same model SEC evidence,
and let a program decide:

15
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,700
nine in ten — on held-out
claims, 240 of 266.

16
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:50,866
Here's how.

17
00:00:50,866 --> 00:00:54,342
Meta's Muse Spark reads the post, extracts

18
00:00:54,342 --> 00:00:58,233
each claim and chooses
which SEC lookup to run.

19
00:00:58,233 --> 00:01:02,400
Python does the arithmetic
and returns the verdict.

20
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:05,700
The model proposes; the program decides.

21
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,300
Live, on the site.

22
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,233
Paste the post and run it.

23
00:01:27,066 --> 00:01:30,066
Muse Spark calls the SEC tools
— every call is on the record.

24
00:01:30,066 --> 00:01:31,000
Contradicted, with the filing.

25
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,466
Here is the corrected draft;
cost and time are on the receipt.

26
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:11,666
The same checks run in batch from the
command line — text, screenshots through

27
00:02:11,666 --> 00:02:16,133
Muse OCR, audio through
Muse Voice Transcribe.

28
00:02:16,133 --> 00:02:21,066
On saved Threads posts,
the median was 6.8 seconds.

29
00:02:21,066 --> 00:02:27,700
At that median, a thousand posts
take about two hours on one worker.

30
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,833
Ninety point two percent
on held-out claims.

31
00:02:31,833 --> 00:02:35,366
It wrongly says 'supported' once in 139.

32
00:02:35,366 --> 00:02:38,333
Two cents and ten seconds a claim.

33
00:02:38,333 --> 00:02:43,700
On real posts, coverage is
reported separately from accuracy.

34
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Every number, checked against the filing.

35
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:57,700
hackathon dot dappgo dot com.

